        "id": "fa0ba06a"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Why savoury, not nuts\n",
        "\n",
        "**Nuts & Seeds** has the better hit rate — 56% of the category already clears the bar — but it\n",
        "is 1.8% of the aisle and only ~1,650 products. It proves the profile is achievable; it is not a\n",
        "platform.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Chips & Savoury** has 6,126 products in the blue ocean, nearly 4× the volume. More\n",
        "importantly: **17,370 of its products (68%) sit in \"Low Sugar, Low Protein.\"** They have already\n",
        "solved sugar. The distance from there to the blue ocean is a few grams of protein — versus\n",
        "asking a chocolate manufacturer to strip 35g of sugar from a bar and keep it edible.\n",
        "\n",
        "The products already there are telling: Scrocchi, Bake rolls, Vollkorn Sticks, Crackers apéritif\n",
        "nature. These are crackers and breadsticks whose 10–12g protein comes from wheat gluten\n",
        "*incidentally*. Nobody formulated them as protein snacks — they are in the blue ocean by\n",
        "accident, with no health positioning behind them.\n",
        "\n",
        "**The gap is not capability. It is assortment.**\n",
        "\n",
        "## 🎯 Key Insight\n",
        "\n",
        "> **Based on the data, the biggest market opportunity is in Savoury Snacks (chips & crackers),\n",
        "> specifically targeting products with 15g of protein and less than 5g of sugar.**\n",
        "\n",
        "15g is the 75th percentile of products *already succeeding* in this quadrant (median 12.3g) — an\n",
        "empirically achievable target, not an aspiration. Under 5g of sugar is comfortably above the\n",
        "quadrant's median of 2.3g.\n",
        "\n",
        "**The whitespace:** deliberately formulated, branded, high-protein savoury snacking. The\n",
        "category is proven by 6,126 products, mass-market at 25,541 products, and has no branded\n",
        "incumbent."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "62101981",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "62101981"
      },
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "# Candidate's Choice: Stress-testing the recommendation\n",
        "\n",
        "**Why I added this.** Story 4 says *where* the gap is. It does not say whether the gap is real\n",
        "or whether the recommendation survives contact with the outside world. Two questions a client\n",
        "asks immediately, neither of which the brief requires me to answer:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **If this space is so attractive, is someone already quietly winning it?**\n",
        "2. **Would the product I am recommending actually look healthy to a consumer?**\n",
        "\n",
        "Both are tested below. The first came back negative — I have kept it in, because a hypothesis\n",
        "that fails is still evidence, and reporting only the tests that worked would misrepresent the\n",
        "analysis.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Test 1: Is the blue ocean owned by retailer own-brand?\n",
        "\n",
        "**Hypothesis:** the top brands in the high-protein savoury quadrant are supermarket labels\n",
        "(Carrefour, Auchan, Picard, Casino, U), which would suggest retailers have quietly filled a gap\n",
        "the big manufacturers ignored."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "uYY2G-6oFb2g",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "uYY2G-6oFb2g"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "PRIVATE_LABEL = [\n",
        "    'carrefour','auchan','casino','leader price','picard','monoprix','franprix',\n",
        "    'lidl','aldi','tesco','sainsbury','asda','morrisons','marks & spencer',\n",
        "    'migros','coop','delhaize','albert heijn','edeka','rewe','conad','esselunga',\n",
        "    'eroski','mercadona','dia','intermarché','netto','penny','u ','super u','systeme u',\n",
        "]\n",
        "\n",
        "def is_private_label(b):\n",
        "    b = str(b).lower()\n",
        "    return any(p in b for p in PRIVATE_LABEL)\n",
        "\n",
        "chips = eu[eu.primary_category == 'Chips & Savoury'].copy()\n",
        "chips['private_label'] = chips['brands'].apply(is_private_label)\n",
        "\n",
        "pl = (chips.groupby('quadrant')['private_label']\n",
        "           .agg(products='size', private_label_share='mean')\n",
        "           .round(3)\n",
        "           .sort_values('products', ascending=False))\n",
        "print(\"Private-label penetration by quadrant — Chips & Savoury\\n\")\n",
        "print(pl)"
      ]
