      "id": "46558994",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "46558994"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Test 1 result: hypothesis rejected\n",
        "\n",
        "**Private-label penetration is essentially flat across all four quadrants (12–16%).** The blue\n",
        "ocean is not retailer territory. Own-brand is no more likely to sit there than in the sugar trap.\n",
        "\n",
        "The concentration check is equally flat: the **top 10 brands account for 9.0% of the blue ocean\n",
        "and 8.4% of the sugar trap.** Whatever explains the gap, it is not that someone is already\n",
        "winning it — and fragmentation is not distinctive to the opportunity, it is just what this\n",
        "category looks like.\n",
        "\n",
        "**What this test does establish**, weakly: the largest single brand in the blue ocean is\n",
        "Carrefour with 78 products — **1.3% of 6,126** — and no global snack manufacturer appears in the\n",
        "top 15 at all. There is no incumbent to displace.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Why the test could not do more.** Open Food Facts is a *product census*, not a sales panel. It\n",
        "records that a product exists; it records nothing about volume, shelf facings, or revenue. A\n",
        "brand with 78 SKUs might dominate the category or might be invisible in it. Brand concentration\n",
        "in this dataset cannot answer a market-share question, and I should have recognised that before\n",
        "running it rather than after.\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## Test 2: Would the recommended product look healthy on the shelf?\n",
        "\n",
        "**The risk.** I am recommending savoury snacks. Savoury means salt. The EU's Nutri-Score\n",
        "algorithm penalises salt heavily. If high-protein crackers score C or D, the client builds a\n",
        "product that is nutritionally sound and *looks unhealthy on the front of the pack* — a\n",
        "commercial problem the nutrient matrix cannot see, because salt is not on either axis.\n",
        "\n",
        "`nutriscore_grade` has been carried through the pipeline since ingestion and is not used\n",
        "anywhere else in this analysis. It is an independent, externally-defined judgement of the exact\n",
        "products I am recommending."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "af45ce74",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "af45ce74"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "scored = eu[eu['nutriscore_grade'].notna() &\n",
